description:
London Borough of Hillingdon and the Zoological Society of London are working together to develop a river enhancement project to improve the section oftheYeading Brook West that flows through Spider Park (Bridgwater Open Space)
Therefore, the London Borough of Hillingdon invited tenders from suitably qualified and experienced contractors to deliver the river enhancement project. Yeading Brook has unnaturally steep banks with little habitat diversity. The aims of river enhancement project where to;
- Reprofile / recontour riverbanks to create key habitats and improve the diversity the environment and its species;
- Contribute to reducing the peak levels and in turn, reduce the flood risk to local residents;
- Increase the ability ofthe riverto adapt and cope with the likely impact of increased intense storms resulting from climate change;
- provide more space for water and slow the flow of wate rto the Yeading Brook further helping to protect people, species and habitats by making them less vulnerable to the effects of climate change
- Create a tranquil spot for observing nature, such as dragonflies, butterflies birds and amphibians, attracted to these new and enhanced habitats.

The London Borough of Hillingdon (the Council) was seeking  to appoint a single supplier for its Lost and Stray Dogs Service, inclusive of collection, transportation and the kennelling of the animals for a period of up to 7 days. The required service is for 24 hours a day, 7 days a week and is to include banned breedsin accordance with the Dangerous Dogs Act 1991.
The following provisions are to be implemented during the contract period:
- Environmental Protection Act 1990;
- Environmental Protection (Stray Dogs) Regulations 1992;
- AnimalWelfare Act 2006;
- The AnimalWelfare (Licensing of Activities involving Animals) Regulations 2018;
- Welfare of Animals (Transport) (England
The contract start date is 1st July 2025 for three years.
Contract start date amended from October 24 to July 25 ( as per previously advertised in the Contract Finder Opportunity Notice ( tender_441996/1363765)

Hillingdon Council had secured funding from Central Government via the GLA, from the UK Shared Prosperity Fund (UKSPF) and was looking to provide a programme of support to the boroughs SME businesses.Specifically, the Council had be awarded funding to deliver UKSPF priority E23: &quot;Strengthening local entrepreneurial ecosystems and supporting businesses at all stages of their development to start, sustain, grow, and innovate, including through local networks&quot;
In addition to providing direct business support, our objective is to understand Hillingdon&#039;s economy better so that we can direct resources to support local businesses and attract appropriate inward investment.
To achieve this, the Council was looking to secure a partner to assist the Council with its statistical and analytic requirements relating to the borough&#039;s economy.
